{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Going forth and returning.</b> Going and circling around the ark, and it did not go on his mission — for he suspected it concerning its mate, as we learned in Aggadat Cheilek (Sanhedrin 108)." "<b>Until the waters dried up.</b> Its plain sense is as it sounds. But the midrash aggadah: the raven was destined for another mission, the withholding of rain in the days of Elijah, as it is said ״וְהָעֹרְבִים מְבִיאִים לוֹ לֶחֶם וּבָשָׂר״ (1 Kings 17)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:56.437364968Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}